author zichuanxu <zichuanxu28@gmail.com> 1790711282 +0900
committer zichuanxu <zichuanxu28@gmail.com> 1790711282 +0900

Paper generators for stage 4: macros, five tables and the predicted-vs-observed figure come from staged run data

Every stage-4 quantity of prereg v2 §8 is generated (paper_numbers, paper_tables, figures) from the
staged analyses named in paper/results_sources.json, through the shared views in
analysis/paper_data.py; a stage that has not run renders as the MISSING marker and a verdict over a
whole set (families, systems, switches) only once the set is complete.

- Macros (Rep, RepPool, Synth, MOne, MTwo, MThree, Nat, Rend, Rank): block R from
  analysis.replication and analysis.gate applied to the committed stage-2 and replication JSON (no
  stage step needed), block C from e1_metrics (C1-C4 with verdicts, program statistics), M1 from
  the merged E2, M2 from families.json, M3 from e7 theta_r_by_reader, N from e5_natives with its
  stage4 summary and e5_cost, L from rendered.json, section 6 from rank_corr.json.
- Tables tab_replication, tab_construct, tab_native, tab_families, tab_rendered; figure
  fig_native_systems (vector PDF, Okabe-Ito, Mem0 falls back to stage 3, other systems show as
  not run).
- New stage kind `m2` (E1 plus analysis/families.json); e7.analyse groups theta_r runs by the reader
  model in each run's manifest (theta_r_by_reader) so that several readers do not mix.
- paper/generated/* regenerated (existing macros and tables unchanged); the paper builds.
- tests/test_paper_stage4.py: MISSING rendering, determinism, complete synthetic inputs (every macro
  reads an existing key; macros and tables compile), real analyses as fixtures, and a check that
  the committed generated files are current.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
